{"step_index":160,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T02:13:38Z","thinking":"The large Excel file presents a challenge due to its size and formatting. A fast search for \"비전조이\" within the file is needed. Considering that `.xlsx` files are essentially zip archives, the `xl/sharedStrings.xml` file within likely contains all text strings. Employing PowerShell with either `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` or zip archive handling should enable rapid search, potentially completing the task within a few seconds, even with millions of rows.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"powershell -Command \"\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem;\n$files = Get-ChildItem 'data\\*.xlsx';\nforeach ($f in $files) {\n    Write-Host 'Checking:' $f.FullName;\n    $zip = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::OpenRead($f.FullName);\n    $entry = $zip.GetEntry('xl/sharedStrings.xml');\n    if ($entry) {\n        $stream = $entry.Open();\n        $reader = New-Object System.IO.StreamReader($stream);\n        $content = $reader.ReadToEnd();\n        $stream.Close();\n        if ($content.Contains('비전조이')) {\n            Write-Host 'Found 비전조이 in' $f.Name;\n        }\n        if ($content.Contains('이구창')) {\n            Write-Host 'Found 이구창 in' $f.Name;\n        }\n        if ($content.Contains('747-6799')) {\n            Write-Host 'Found 747-6799 in' $f.Name;\n        }\n    }\n    $zip.Dispose();\n}\nWrite-Host 'Done checking excel files.';\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\worktrees\\resilient-bardeen\\add_vision_joy_data","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Fast search in xlsx sharedStrings"}}]}
